        "AbstractText": "Novel quadruple stimuli-responsive mechanized silica nanoparticles were constructed by installation of supramolecular nanovalves onto the exterior surface of mesoporous silica nanoparticles. The release of cargo molecules is triggered by acid/Zn2+ /alkali/reduction potential stimuli. This has potential application in the development of drug delivery systems or construction of smart anticorrosion coatings."
